WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.840
The next choice is where

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.560
you want to use your

3
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.240
Continuum context.

4
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.840
Your working history stays in

5
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.280
the folder you chose.

6
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.120
Connecting an AI tool gives

7
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.400
it directions for finding that

8
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.400
history and your personal guide.

9
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.600
It doesn't copy your whole

10
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.040
library into the tool.

11
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.080
For a local tool such

12
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.920
as Codex or Claude Code,

13
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.600
the setup assistant adds those

14
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.120
directions to the project you

15
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.160
choose.

16
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.760
It then checks whether the

17
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.200
tool can actually find your

18
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.480
context there.

19
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.320
Creating the files alone doesn't

20
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.160
mean every conversation in every

21
00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.680
app can use them.

22
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.440
A web project works differently.

23
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.880
The portable option gives you

24
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.960
readable context files to upload.

25
00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.680
Think of these as a

26
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.520
snapshot of your personal guide.

27
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:44.570
The web chat

28
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.480
can use the uploaded information,

29
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:53.600
but it doesn't gain a

30
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.880
live connection to the history

31
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.400
on your Mac.

32
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.320
When that guide changes, you'll

33
00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.680
need to refresh the uploaded

34
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:00.510
copy.

35
00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.110
Corrections made on the web

36
00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.550
also need a supported way

37
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:05.310
back into Continuum, such as

38
00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.040
a later conversation export.

39
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.190
Whichever route you choose, the

40
00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.190
context an AI reads is

41
00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:19.080
shared with that AI service.

42
00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.270
You can start with one

43
00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.750
destination and add another later.

44
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.030
Would you like to connect

45
00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:36.270
this tool, both local tools,

46
00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.710
or make a portable copy

47
00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.350
for a web project?
